<body><h1>Kiểm tra sandbox CLB Báo Chí</h1><div id="results"><pre class="ok">ok S04 matches hand calculation including fatigue</pre><pre class="ok">ok fatigue, Q boundaries, and failed interview values</pre><pre class="ok">ok equipment thresholds remain unlocked after reputation falls</pre><pre class="ok">ok fixture data is deterministic: 96 subjects, eight each week</pre><pre class="ok">ok subject lifetime is five days and upcoming subjects cannot be scouted</pre><pre class="ok">ok scouting costs energy, reveals fixed truth, and cannot be repeated</pre><pre class="ok">ok interview consumes energy and fatigue exactly once, preserving original state</pre><pre class="ok">ok assignment rejects duplicate staff, locked staff, insufficient energy</pre><pre class="ok">ok solo support works with one available Khue, at half support stat</pre><pre class="ok">ok failed interview spends attention and fatigue, creates zero-value unpublished article</pre><pre class="ok">ok night recovery resets energy and availability; weekend adds extra recovery</pre><pre class="ok">ok grit is editable until publication, Q and fatigue do not change</pre><pre class="ok">ok only published articles add evidence and pressure</pre><pre class="ok">ok selection rejects unknown, duplicate, failed, and more than four articles</pre><pre class="ok">ok paper sorts slots and computes weights rather than drag order</pre><pre class="ok">ok article and paper scores are capped; van penalty applies after paper cap</pre><pre class="ok">ok van absence counts all attempted work, including unpublished failures, capped at 25%</pre><pre class="ok">ok empty and failed slots reduce reputation; a blank issue gets extra penalty</pre><pre class="ok">ok scheduled strikes use 40% and 80% boundaries; emergency is &gt;= threshold</pre><pre class="ok">ok emergency strike carries 30%, increases difficulty and suspends next issue only</pre><pre class="ok">ok consecutive heavy strikes preserve suspension and difficulty caps at two</pre><pre class="ok">ok pre-strike reputation can unlock equipment despite later strike penalty</pre><pre class="ok">ok endings require both thresholds, evidence alone is bitter</pre><pre class="ok">ok two zero-reputation weeks disband early and stop actions</pre><pre class="ok">ok cannot close a week early; day 60 concludes the semester without day 61 actions</pre><pre class="ok">ok save roundtrip retains edits, assignments, config and reports under separate namespace</pre><pre class="ok">ok save rejects legacy, malformed, future-version, and out-of-range state</pre><pre class="ok">ok storage failures propagate instead of reporting successful saves</pre><pre class="ok">ok sandbox validates state and config patches and logs explicit edits</pre><pre class="ok">ok auto day uses game actions, scouting does not see future subjects</pre><pre class="ok">ok all eight strategies terminate deterministically with valid week reports</pre><pre class="ok">ok comparison honors modified roster join dates without changing source roster</pre><pre class="ok">ok content: active pack validates; dangling maps and dialogue references fail</pre><pre class="ok">ok text: parameters, fallback and historical log messages resolve without changing event data</pre><pre class="ok">ok session: failed commands and invalid replacements leave the current state intact</pre><pre class="ok">ok world input: routing respects blocking and releases every listener on disposal</pre><pre class="ok">ok saves: versioned roundtrip, v1 migration, isolated modes and storage failures</pre><pre class="ok">ok real map UI: assign, interview, edit, publish, save/load and map station</pre><pre class="ok">ok real sandbox UI: patch state, tune roster, auto week, compare and change config</pre><pre class="ok">ok gameplay: interview costs energy, info opens before whole-case assignment, immutable transition</pre><pre class="ok">ok gameplay: bed blocks day transition, zero-energy approval, work processed once</pre><pre class="ok">ok gameplay: mismatch raises day one, reassignment restarts, loss is one working day</pre><pre class="ok">ok gameplay: Friday assignments pause Saturday/Sunday and resume Monday</pre><pre class="ok">ok gameplay: editorial work pauses on weekends and late writing rolls to next issue</pre><pre class="ok">ok gameplay: outside investigation uses separate slot energy and cannot become extra free activity</pre><pre class="ok">ok gameplay: Khue needs distinct verified steps, writes own article, no double packaging multiplier</pre><pre class="ok">ok gameplay: gifts cannot bypass events, romance requires affirmative choice</pre><pre class="ok">ok gameplay: betrayal reduces stats only for current female romantic partners</pre><pre class="ok">ok gameplay: matching base roster completes stories without upgrade or tool</pre><pre class="ok">ok gameplay: only one consumable boost per day, money and tools enforce cost</pre><pre class="ok">ok gameplay: mock ending requires both branches, two-week playthroughs finish all calendar days</pre><pre class="ok">ok gameplay real UI: map activity, feedback modal, free approval, sleep and isolated save</pre><pre class="ok">ok anime sprite atlas: 84 nonempty transparent frames, feet aligned, direction and walk poses distinct</pre><pre class="ok">ok pixel maps: all doors and interaction points are reachable; destination spawns are safe</pre><pre class="ok">ok pixel collision: wall, water, furniture and NPC tiles reject movement; paths never skip tiles</pre><pre class="ok">ok pixel NPC schedule: club during school hours, leisure after club and weekends, future joins hidden</pre><pre class="ok">ok pixel saves: invalid/out-of-bounds/blocked positions fall back to walkable spawn</pre><pre class="ok">ok pixel real UI: assets, keyboard, collision, walk through four maps, NPC/board, job, bed feedback and position save</pre><pre class="ok">ok pilot Khuê/Vân and storyboard candidate: 192 frames, binary alpha, shared limited palette, matched neutral height and fixed canvas</pre><pre class="ok">ok Khue up/down walk preserves idle upper proportions; idle/talk and sideways walk stay unchanged</pre><pre class="ok">ok pilot clips: distance-driven walk keeps phase across time/direction, variable idle durations and fallback</pre><pre class="ok">ok sprite lab real UI: all clips/directions, pause/step, onion skin, zoom and mobile containment</pre><pre class="ok">ok walk storyboards: four views retain anatomical contact, draw real poses and synchronize pause/step controls</pre><pre class="ok">ok dialogue art: nine identities, 24 transparent assets and registered pose groups load</pre><pre class="ok">ok dialogue renderer: latest speaker wins, failed expression falls back to neutral, rerender reuses loaded image</pre><pre class="ok">ok dialogue lab real UI: identity/expression selection and mobile buttons remain visible</pre><pre class="ok">ok interaction scenes: every choice resolves, all nine identities and 24 expressions are reachable</pre><pre class="ok">ok interaction map real UI: walk to all actors, branch conversations, restore movement and render mobile</pre><pre class="ok">ok coastal gallery: mobile portrait/choices, long text and reduced-motion CSS/JS</pre><pre class="ok">ok coastal overlays: trap focus, retain dialog, dismiss policy, unlock and restore focus</pre><pre class="ok">ok coastal dialogue: stable reading surface and portrait, latest update and disposal</pre><pre class="ok">ok coastal pixel shell: preserves world/HUD identity, overlay lock and mobile menu</pre><p class="ok">72/72 passed</p><pre id="dialogue-art-audit">[
